{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1048606-urban-shadows","id":1048606,"title":"Urban Shadows","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-02-13T23:39:21-08:00","id":1048606,"title":"Urban Shadows","content":"Since it scratches a very similar itch to World/Chronicles of Darkness, I figured I'd ask here: how do folks like Urban Shadows? For the unfamiliar, it's a Powered by the Apocalypse game about monsters and in-the-know mortals making shady deals and terrible mistakes in the back alleys of a world very much like our own.<br /> <br /> I've never played a PbtA game before and would like Urban Shadows to be my first, but I'm deterred from it by the promise of later content that was funded by the Kickstarter (two years ago!) that still isn't out yet; the weird completionist in me doesn't want to get into it before all the options are out. Supposedly the setting book is going to be out in the next month or so, but I have my doubts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T01:06:37-08:00","id":1052441,"title":"","content":"Hey atamajakki,<br /> <br /> I actually got Urban Shadows as a present from a friend of mine who attended a Con. I've been slowly making my way trough the book and I've been really liking it so far.<br /> <br /> The system is very simplified in all the right ways, and it's primary engagement comes from trying to figure out the most creative way to use Moves to tell the story you want for your character. Corruption Moves are a cool idea although some of them seem a bit strange in how they trigger (like the Aware Archtype makes perfect sense from an engaging narrative perspective but the Veteran Archetype's &quot;don't head straight into danger&quot; trigger seems like it would make the character less engaging rather than more.)<br /> <br /> Again, still going through the book so I can't give you a full picture of it yet. But, just to some up one of my favorite parts: Urban Shadows simplifies and condenses Kindred Politics and Economics into a single unique feature all Vampires get called The Web, without sacrificing all the creativity and depravity that comes from the original source material. It's really a thing of beauty and really showed to me that this was definitly a product to look more into. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T15:51:30-08:00","id":1054492,"title":"","content":"It looks like a really lovely game, but it drives me up the wall when games have more content coming that I want. Their Kickstarter funded in June 2014, and we're now nearly into March 2017 without their one supplement still coming out - and that supplement still isn't going to have all the stretch goal Archetypes! I understand that books take time, but those playbooks are literally three pages long, and the hold up worries me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T03:17:20-08:00","id":1054695,"title":"","content":"Really?<br /> <br /> I wasn't really aware of the information about it's Kickstarter history, so I wasn't even sure what extra content was coming. My only experience with it has been as a present from a friend, so I completely understand your reservations about picking it up. I'd most likely have them too were I in your shoes.<br /> <br /> Just curious too now, what stuff is in the content they're supposed to release?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T08:38:39-08:00","id":1054767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1048606-urban-shadows?p=1054695#post1054695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really?<br /> <br /> I wasn't really aware of the information about it's Kickstarter history, so I wasn't even sure what extra content was coming. My only experience with it has been as a present from a friend, so I completely understand your reservations about picking it up. I'd most likely have them too were I in your shoes.<br /> <br /> Just curious too now, what stuff is in the content they're supposed to release?</div> </div> </div> </div>A supplement called Dark Streets, with some prebuilt settings and playbooks, and then three or four other playbooks past that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T12:27:59-08:00","id":1054909,"title":"","content":"Oh, nice. Gonna check this one out. Thanks for the tip.<br /> <br /> Edit: Shit. Have you ever been in that situation when you were going to buy an RPG and bought four?<br /> <br /> *sigh* I have a problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":75,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","user":"Weimann","date":". 02-25-2017, 04:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T16:40:11-08:00","id":1054993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1048606-urban-shadows?p=1054767#post1054767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A supplement called Dark Streets, with some prebuilt settings and playbooks, and then three or four other playbooks past that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Damn, I though it was maybe just one or two...and they're all still not coming out yet and have no specified release date?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T16:50:20-08:00","id":1054996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1048606-urban-shadows?p=1054993#post1054993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Damn, I though it was maybe just one or two...and they're all still not coming out yet and have no specified release date?</div> </div> </div> </div>They said &quot;end of this month!&quot; last month for Dark Streets, and nebulously further out than that for the other playbooks. <br /> <br /> It wouldn't bug me so much if those playbooks - The Angel, The Immortal, The Dragon - didn't all sound like characters I'd kill to play as, or if that city book didn't have my RPG author crush Ken Hite describing his beloved home of Chicago in it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T17:34:50-08:00","id":1055010,"title":"","content":"Geeeeh! I want all of those things! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Damnit Urban Shadows!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T05:21:24-08:00","id":1055180,"title":"","content":"I've played it and I'm a big fan. Our campaign involved a ghost (my character), a werewolf, and immortal, a chaos mage, and a chosen one (I think that's what they're called). A narrative heavy, systems light game. Very enjoyable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T19:49:57-08:00","id":1055510,"title":"","content":"That's fantastic, i'm glad you got to play a game of Urban Shadows. I've been wanting to for some time but haven't got a chance due to my usual group having a more difficult time meeting up thanks to distance and work. <br /> <br /> How was using the Moves in actual play? Was is very fluid and not noticeable or does it have a bit of a different feel from how other horror or dark fantasy games usually run?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T22:26:02-08:00","id":1055541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1048606-urban-shadows?p=1055180#post1055180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've played it and I'm a big fan. Our campaign involved a ghost (my character), a werewolf, and immortal, a chaos mage, and a chosen one (I think that's what they're called). A narrative heavy, systems light game. Very enjoyable.</div> </div> </div> </div>That got me thinking: are there any contemporary non-storygame-type (I mean in a sense of not having direct narrative-influencing mechanics), medium-crunch/simulationist alternatives to WoD/CofD 1e for urban fantasy/horror games? Excluding CoC.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T00:10:52-08:00","id":1055555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1048606-urban-shadows?p=1055541#post1055541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That got me thinking: are there any contemporary non-storygame-type (I mean in a sense of not having direct narrative-influencing mechanics), medium-crunch/simulationist alternatives to WoD/CofD 1e for urban fantasy/horror games? Excluding CoC.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose my answer depends on whether or not you think GUMSHOE counts as a storygame, but then again storygame isn't a dirty word for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T15:09:19-08:00","id":1055818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1048606-urban-shadows?p=1055555#post1055555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I suppose my answer depends on whether or not you think GUMSHOE counts as a storygame, but then again storygame isn't a dirty word for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it's a dirty word either. It's just not my cup of tea, for various reasons.<br /> <br /> It seems like that most new games nowadays either belong to the D&amp;D/OSR family, or are indie/storygames and the urban fantasy/horror games I know about are from to the latter group which I'm not really interested in (although some of the settings are really interesting, it's just the mechanical approach I don't like).<br /> <br /> It would be great to have alternatives with the classical style of WoD/NWoD 1e as approach to system goes and I thought someone might know a game I'm not aware of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T16:38:37-08:00","id":1055867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1048606-urban-shadows?p=1055818#post1055818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think it's a dirty word either. It's just not my cup of tea, for various reasons.<br /> <br /> It seems like that most new games nowadays either belong to the D&amp;D/OSR family, or are indie/storygames and the urban fantasy/horror games I know about are from to the latter group which I'm not really interested in (although some of the settings are really interesting, it's just the mechanical approach I don't like).<br /> <br /> It would be great to have alternatives with the classical style of WoD/NWoD 1e as approach to system goes and I thought someone might know a game I'm not aware of.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you want an alternative to CoC and nWoD mortals, definitely give Fear Itself/The Esoterrorists a look. I'm not sure if you'll dislike it or not (some folks have a vehement hatred of GUMSHOE, viewing it as fixing a problem that doesn't exist) but it's my favorite horror investigative game on the market.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T17:13:00-08:00","id":1055886,"title":"","content":"Ok, thanks, I read up on them a little and they both seem promising, especially Esoterrorists!<br /> <br /> Also, could anyone say something about GURPS Horror? I knew about GURPS, but never delved into it 'til now. The new Discworld book immediately got me interested, since, hey, Discworld! I always wanted to play Discworld! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Although it seemed contradictory with the kind of game GURPS is. *<br /> As far as I understand GURPS might be on the higher end of simulationism, but I'm okay with games like Pathfinder and Shadowrun, although my favorite systems are really the middle-ground ones, like WoD.<br /> <br /> *giving it a second thought, it actually makes sense. Aside from all the obvious silliness and humor of Pratchett's books and world, he actually wrote in a fairly sensible way. His description of fights, injuries, etc. are quite realistic opposed to the average heroic fantasy style and even the magic is working along things like conservation of matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":6363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","user":"PM\u00e1rk","date":". 02-27-2017, 08:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T18:48:18-08:00","id":1055940,"title":"","content":"I've have some friends who had some bad experiences with GURPS, but that might just have been an instance of having a bad GM. Also, is there really a discworld supplement for GURPS?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T19:05:14-08:00","id":1055943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1048606-urban-shadows?p=1055940#post1055940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Also, is there really a discworld supplement for GURPS?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes Virginia.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.sjgames.com/gurps/books/Discworld/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.sjgames.com/navbar/eiphome.gif\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.sjgames.com/gurps/books/Discworld/\" target=\"_blank\"> Discworld Roleplaying Game </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.sjgames.com/gurps/books/Discworld/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.sjgames.com/gurps/books/Discworld/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T19:32:22-08:00","id":1055951,"title":"","content":"Ha! Nice. Will definitly need to give that a look over later. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T19:34:32-08:00","id":1055952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1048606-urban-shadows?p=1055940#post1055940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've have some friends who had some bad experiences with GURPS, but that might just have been an instance of having a bad GM. Also, is there really a discworld supplement for GURPS?</div> </div> </div> </div>More than that, it's an all-standalone book, with all the rules and fluff from the earlier editions' supplements for DW! I really don't know how it eluded me so long. It's not even that pricey and certainly not for that size and amount of content.<br /> <br /> As far as I cobbled together from some reading of reddit and stuff, most of the complaints for GURPS are due to it's toolbox nature, namely that you have to understand it and put work into it to know what to and not to use. Although the Discworld book seems to be an exception, since it's an all-in. Also, the sim-style is certainly not for everyone. I reserve judgment until played it, but... to the hell with it, it has Discworld! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also, after some reading, the horror supplement for 4e is generally praised, so it seems.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T21:23:55-08:00","id":1055980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1048606-urban-shadows?p=1055952#post1055952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> More than that, it's an all-standalone book, with all the rules and fluff from the earlier editions' supplements for DW! I really don't know how it eluded me so long. It's not even that pricey and certainly not for that size and amount of content.<br /> <br /> As far as I cobbled together from some reading of reddit and stuff, most of the complaints for GURPS are due to it's toolbox nature, namely that you have to understand it and put work into it to know what to and not to use. Although the Discworld book seems to be an exception, since it's an all-in. Also, the sim-style is certainly not for everyone. I reserve judgment until played it, but... to the hell with it, it has Discworld! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also, after some reading, the horror supplement for 4e is generally praised, so it seems.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Not to be a jerk, but this is scarcely about Urban Shadows, is it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T21:32:55-08:00","id":1055983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1048606-urban-shadows?p=1055980#post1055980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not to be a jerk, but this is scarcely about Urban Shadows, is it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I figured it went into a quite off-topic direction, so I didn't plan to write more about it. I might start a new topic tomorrow.<br /> <br /> Anyway, thanks for the heads-up on GUMSHOE!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T21:21:15-08:00","id":1056463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1048606-urban-shadows?p=1055983#post1055983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, I figured it went into a quite off-topic direction, so I didn't plan to write more about it. I might start a new topic tomorrow.<br /> <br /> Anyway, thanks for the heads-up on GUMSHOE!</div> </div> </div> </div>Let me know when you start that topic, I have a ton of GURPS books, so I can give some input.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T05:38:05-08:00","id":1056586,"title":"","content":"I've now given Urban Shadows a first read, and I'm excited. There seems to be a few more knobs to twist when it comes to mechanical player choices than is usually the case with Apocalypse World Engine mechanics, which appeals to me. The idea of having two different progression systems with different implications is also interesting. I feel like it takes some significant strides in shaping the PbtA mechanics for the future.<br /> <br /> Tangentially related, <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/medeiros/the-watch-rpg\" target=\"_blank\">I just now came across another Kickstarter where the same author is involved</a>. It's about a group of female soldiers fighting an invading darkness in a low-fantasy setting. The OP had some issues with the fulfilment of the Urban Shadows Kickstarter, so consider that, but I think the theme of the idea looks kind of cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T22:50:10-08:00","id":1057474,"title":"","content":"So thanks to a slightly uncomfortable brush with someone claiming to be Magpie Games' layout person on Reddit, I found out that Dark Streets is apparently due out this coming month (yay!) and that he has no release window for the other playbooks, with The Angel described as &quot;a long term thing&quot; (boo!). This game is an absolute treat, but not having all of the content is aggravating the completionist in me beyond words.<br /> <br /> I have to say, after a decade+ immersed in WoD/CofD, it's sort of refreshing to have a game say &quot;vampires exist, they drink blood, go&quot; and have that be the end of it. The minimalist approach that PbtA and especially US embodies takes some getting used to, but is really effective.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T01:49:41-08:00","id":1057497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1048606-urban-shadows?p=1057474#post1057474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to say, after a decade+ immersed in WoD/CofD, it's sort of refreshing to have a game say &quot;vampires exist, they drink blood, go&quot; and have that be the end of it. The minimalist approach that PbtA and especially US embodies takes some getting used to, but is really effective.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it's nice that &quot;use any reasonable power&quot; is just a single basic move, for exampe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-10T13:51:45-08:00","id":1061009,"title":"","content":"Here here, <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Read a little bit more myself while trying to not go over our internet data usage and really love the minimalist approach they did to all of the Archetypes. It hit's that just right level of negative space where it's like a blank piece of paper just ready to be turned into something beautiful, or at least interesting depending on how good your own ideas and art skills are that is. <br /> <br /> My only complaint is that while the corruption mechanics are neat, they do sort of have the WoD Morality problem with some of the Archetypes. I feel a more slippery slop into obsession and ultimately a cruel and doomed fate would work better as a way to describe corruption, but I do understand why they wrote it up as they did.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T09:16:52-07:00","id":1066932,"title":"","content":"It seems <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/206665/Urban-Shadows-Dark-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">Dark Streets</a> has been released.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T14:28:19-07:00","id":1127331,"title":"","content":"Minor necro on this, but I just started an Urban Shadows campaign a few days ago! It's set in my hometown of sunny San Diego, which I had a lot of fun writing up; there's a lot of local strangeness to play with in a fantasy context. My players made a demonic deal-broker working at a local startup run by Belphegor, a psychic vampire who runs a lesbian bar, a Canadian monster hunter who pays the bills as a fake ghost hunter, and an amnesiac ghost trying to find her murderer. The plot is currently shaping up to an attempt to stop the fae of the Summer Court from prolonging their season by starting a wildfire that will consume the whole city, but it's going to get a lot weirder than that...<br /> <br /> Also, the last two Kickstarter playbooks (The Immortal and The Dragon) are apparently due out this month to backers! I'm super jealous of anyone who did back; the wait for this has been killing me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T22:55:31-07:00","id":1127494,"title":"","content":"Nice! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I still got to run the game myself one of these times. Got just the group in mind too, just need to work around everyone's crazy scheduels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-04T18:26:49-07:00","id":1137538,"title":"","content":"One of the authors is clearly a Promethean fan, because one playbook (The Vessel) is a construct trying to gain enough Redemption points to become human. It's kind of amazing how well they managed to get everything good about PtC into two pages of mechanics.<br /> <br /> I don't get to play scarcely ever, so I live vicariously through an NPC; Regina, the gargoyle who runs a coffee shop and learns about humanity by eavesdropping. She's going on a date with the psychic vampire PC next session.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-14T13:27:35-07:00","id":1140296,"title":"","content":"Apparently the new playbooks are out to backers now. I'm so jealous!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}